    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Description\n\nAdd `config.hooks = {pre = nil, post = nil}` options. `config.hooks.pre` should be called before (potentially successful?) commenting; `config.hooks.post` - after successful commenting.\r\n\r\nThe most important application is to allow multi-language support through manually adjusting `commentstring` option in `hooks.pre`. See: [JoosepAlviste/nvim-ts-context-commentstring](https://github.com/JoosepAlviste/nvim-ts-context-commentstring) and #50.",
